(vector (map (:db/id -1), (:adr/id "2607242300"), (:adr/title "cloud-itonami-lei-* -- ToSMonitor-LLM/ToSArchiveGovernor actor, round 2: extend from 11 to 21 of ~155 repos"), (:adr/status :accepted), (:adr/date "2026-07-24"), (:adr/doc_type "adr"), (:adr/source-format "edn"), (:adr/related (vector "90-docs/adr/2607241900-cloud-itonami-lei-tos-monitor-actor-pilot.edn" "90-docs/adr/2607242000-cloud-itonami-lei-tos-monitor-actor-batch10.edn" "90-docs/adr/2607110300-cloud-itonami-lei-corporate-tos-catalog.edn")), (:adr/scope-still-not-fleet-wide "this ADR extends the actor layer to 10 MORE cloud-itonami-lei-* repos (21 of ~155 total after this round: the ADR-2607241900 pilot + ADR-2607242000's first 10 + these 10). ~134 repos remain untouched, governed solely by ADR-2607110300. Owner explicitly chose to continue at the same batch-of-10 pace (rather than a larger batch or the full remaining ~144) when asked after round 1 landed clean"), (:adr/batch-companies "cloud-itonami-lei-0eeb8gf0w0npcihzx097 (AECOM, US), cloud-itonami-lei-254900rhl9meus5nkx63 (NextEra Energy Inc, US-FL), cloud-itonami-lei-52990063s23n13hu4e98 (Deutsche Bahn AG, DE -- first :terms-of-carriage doc-type company in this actor family), cloud-itonami-lei-529900s21eq1bo4esm68 (TotalEnergies SE, FR), cloud-itonami-lei-549300de8zaiys2t6q22 (Teekay Tankers Ltd, BM -- first Bermuda-jurisdiction company), cloud-itonami-lei-549300ihyhcqp2pir591 (GATX Corporation, US-NY), cloud-itonami-lei-549300ugkofv2iwjjg27 (TC Energy Corporation, CA-AB -- first Canada-jurisdiction company), cloud-itonami-lei-784f5xwpltwktbv3e584 (The Goldman Sachs Group Inc, US-DE), cloud-itonami-lei-bn6wccz8ovp3ituuvn49 (LyondellBasell Industries N.V., GB), cloud-itonami-lei-luzqvyp4vs22clwdar65 (3M Company, US-DE) -- again an evenly-spread sample of the remaining pool (144 repos after round 1), not cherry-picked"), (:adr/identical-code-per-company "tosmonitor.governor/phase/operation/registry/advisor remain byte-identical across all 21 repos now carrying this actor (unchanged from round 1's already-fixed known-doc-types vocabulary -- no further code bugs surfaced in this round). Only tosmonitor.store's company/baseline demo data, README.md, and docs/adr/0001 differ per repo, same convention as round 1"), (:adr/no-new-bugs-round2 "unlike round 1 (which found and fixed a real source-domain base-domain bug during pilot construction, and a real known-doc-types vocabulary gap surfaced by Brookdale's :terms-of-use), this round's 10 companies -- including a first-of-kind :terms-of-carriage doc-type (Deutsche Bahn), a first Bermuda-jurisdiction entity (Teekay Tankers), and a first Canada-jurisdiction entity (TC Energy) -- all passed lint/test/demo on the first attempt with the round-1-corrected template, no code changes were needed to the byte-identical governor/phase/operation/registry/advisor files"), (:adr/test-status-batch10-round2 "each of the 10 repos independently passes its own governor contract (6 HARD checks + high-stakes/never-auto invariant), phase invariants, store parity (MemStore/DatomicStore), and advisor smoke tests, plus a clean clojure -M:dev:run walkthrough where spot-checked, before being merged -- same bar as round 1 and the original pilot"), (:adr/body "# ADR-2607242300: cloud-itonami-lei-* ToSMonitor round-2 batch-of-10 extension\n\n- Status: Accepted (2026-07-24)\n- Related: ADR-2607241900 (the original 1-repo pilot); ADR-2607242000 (round 1's\n  batch-of-10, which found and fixed two real bugs -- a source-domain base-domain\n  matching bug and a guessed-not-grounded known-doc-types vocabulary gap); ADR-2607110300\n  (the archive-only design still governing the other ~134 repos, unchanged).\n\n## Context\n\nADR-2607242000 landed 10 repos as a validation batch after the ADR-2607241900 pilot,\nexplicitly scoped as 'prove the pattern before deciding whether to extend further.'\nThat round found two genuine bugs a single-repo pilot could not have surfaced\n(a naive base-domain heuristic mismatching sibling subdomains, and a doc-type\nvocabulary that had been guessed rather than grounded in the real archive data),\nboth fixed before/during that round. With 11 of ~155 repos now carrying a real,\ntested governed actor and zero known outstanding defects, the owner asked to\ncontinue expanding ('さらに展開'). Asked about pace, the owner chose to repeat\nthe SAME batch-of-10 size that had just worked cleanly, rather than accelerating\nto a larger batch or the full remaining ~144 repos in one sweep.\n\n## Decision\n\n1. **10 more repos** (21 of ~155 total after this round), again an evenly-spread\n   sample of the remaining pool (not cherry-picked for ease), spanning three\n   NEW firsts for this actor family: Deutsche Bahn AG's `:terms-of-carriage`\n   doc-type (already in the corrected `known-doc-types` set from round 1, so\n   this exercises rather than breaks the fix), Teekay Tankers' Bermuda (`BM`)\n   jurisdiction, and TC Energy's Canada (`CA-AB`) jurisdiction.\n2. **No further code changes needed.** Unlike round 1, this round's `tosmonitor.\n   governor`/`phase`/`operation`/`registry`/`advisor` files were copied verbatim\n   from the round-1-corrected template with zero modifications -- every one of\n   the 10 new companies passed lint/test/(spot-checked) demo on first attempt.\n   This is itself a signal that round 1's two fixes were the real remaining\n   gaps in the pattern, not a partial fix that round 2 would need to extend\n   further.\n3. **Same bar, no relaxation.** Each of the 10 repos still gets its own full\n   governor-contract/phase/store-parity/advisor test suite and its own\n   PR+merge, verified individually.\n4. **Still not fleet-wide.** ~134 `cloud-itonami-lei-*` repos remain untouched,\n   governed solely by ADR-2607110300. Whether to continue beyond this round\n   (same pace, a larger batch, or the full remaining set) is an explicit\n   further decision each time, not implied by this ADR.\n\n## Consequences\n\n- (+) 21/~155 repos (about 14%) now carry a governed actor, with zero known\n  defects remaining in the byte-identical template code after two rounds of\n  real-data validation.\n- (+) Exercised three new jurisdiction/doc-type combinations (Bermuda, Canada,\n  terms-of-carriage) without needing further template changes -- evidence the\n  pattern generalizes beyond the specific companies rounds 1-2 happened to pick.\n- (-) Still requires a human decision point before every further round; no\n  bulk/automated rollout mechanism exists or is being introduced by this ADR.\n- (-) The per-company manual-construction cost (reading each repo's own real\n  blueprint.edn/tos.journal.edn, hand-writing a short representative baseline\n  excerpt, individual PR+merge) does not decrease round over round -- this\n  remains a deliberate choice (owner declined a bulk-generator-script\n  alternative when first asked, ADR-2607242000 Context), not a scaling\n  limitation to be solved later without a further explicit decision.\n\n## References\n\n- ADR-2607241900, ADR-2607242000, ADR-2607110300\n- The 10 repos' own `docs/adr/0001-tos-monitor-actor.md` records\n")))
